The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
err = btf__get_from_id(info.btf_id, &btf);
if (err) {
    p_err("failed to get btf");
    goto err_close;
}
```
Reason:
The unnecessary call to `btf__get_from_id(info.btf_id, &btf)` retrieves a BTF object that is not needed to check if a map has an associated BTF. Since the retrieved BTF object is not freed, this results in a memory leak. Additionally, the error handling logic attempts to close file descriptors in the `err_close` section, which can lead to a double close issue because the calling function `do_dump()` also closes these file descriptors.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
if (err) {
    p_err("can't get map info: %s", strerror(errno));
    return -1;
}
if (!info.btf_id)
    return 0;
```
Reason:
The fix removes the unnecessary retrieval of the BTF object and instead checks if `info.btf_id` is non-zero to determine if a map has an associated BTF. This eliminates the memory leak since no BTF object is allocated, and it also resolves the double close issue by removing the `err_close` section, ensuring that file descriptors are only closed once by the calling function.

